WEBVTT

00:00:09.970 --> 00:00:13.030
Okay, now you're all going to see
the secret of the pendant,

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:17.910
as well as find out what Bruce's legacy really is.

00:00:17.910 --> 00:00:19.280
Franca!

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:28.760
In the vastness of space, there <i>is</i> but one
man ever known <i>as</i> the Pirate King.

00:00:28.760 --> 00:00:32.090
That man, Bruce, left this pendant
to his beloved daughter, Franca.

00:00:32.090 --> 00:00:36.200
Inside it is a memory chip, which was
embedded in his artificial eye.

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:39.010
This chip holds a complete record
of the universe's greatest heist,

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:42.140
a job that was once even said to be impossible:

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:45.700
the robbery of ten billion space dollars
from the Central Bank's vault.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:47.740
Central Bank?!

00:00:47.740 --> 00:00:50.210
I've never heard about any heists like that!

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:54.920
If Central Bank was ever broken into,
it'd be huge news!

00:00:54.920 --> 00:00:57.450
That's exactly why they can't
announce it to the public.

00:00:57.450 --> 00:01:02.360
Central Bank is the backbone and also the very
symbol of the intercosmic financial system.

00:01:02.360 --> 00:01:06.160
They can't have that place going down.

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:10.430
Well, for now, just have a look at this.

00:01:19.610 --> 00:01:23.040
The ship will soon be entering the atmosphere.

00:01:23.040 --> 00:01:27.410
We ask that all passengers please
have your seatbelts fastened.

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:35.760
Hey? You all right, Franca?

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:36.960
Yeah...

00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:39.960
The final exam for Central Bank executive trainees

00:01:39.960 --> 00:01:45.800
will begin at 10:00 am local time
at Central Bank's main facility.

00:02:06.770 --> 00:02:10.160
I etch out today with my finger

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:13.560
on the dusty hood of a car

00:02:13.560 --> 00:02:17.030
As the rain shower passed over

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:19.870
it vanished just like love

00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:25.010
ls there something in your heart

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:27.110
you can't get rid of?

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:33.780
Beat your invisible wings

00:02:33.780 --> 00:02:37.650
We'll fight back against the wind

00:02:37.650 --> 00:02:40.490
that gusts at us so relentlessly

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:43.890
We'll stand firm against it

00:02:43.890 --> 00:02:47.730
with steadfast emotion! Go!

00:02:47.730 --> 00:02:54.640
We continue running on our way

00:02:54.640 --> 00:03:00.640
to a place promised, where sandstorms whirl

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:03.770
Tonight is the night

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:07.280
We're gonna make it through

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:15.000
On to our destination

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:28.730
Looks like we're there.

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:36.730
Episode 4   Bygone Days

00:03:33.170 --> 00:03:36.340
That's a helluva building!

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:40.220
Well, the planet itself is one big bank after all.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:42.780
Except this is the first time for me to see it too.

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:44.690
Photography is prohibited,

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:47.920
and TV or any other kind of coverage
is also off limits.

00:03:48.590 --> 00:03:50.090
Hey, Mister.

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:54.300
We can consider this video to be our
treasure map, right?

00:03:54.300 --> 00:03:57.390
Explain it to them, Swamp.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:01.270
In order to get the information he
needed to pull off the heist,

00:04:01.270 --> 00:04:04.430
Bruce decided to slip into Central Bank first.

00:04:05.470 --> 00:04:09.220
He went in disguise, under 
the assumed identity of "Otis Ray."

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:09.210
Otis Ray Central Bank 
Executive Trainee Exam Pass

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:16.900
QUESTIONS FOR THE 7TH EDITION OF THE CENTRAL BANK EXECUTIVE TRAINEE EXAM
QUESTION 1: Please complete the following program code by filling in the blanks.

00:04:12.510 --> 00:04:14.820
Do you know the answers, Katana?

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:16.150
Why the hell would I know?!

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:17.270
QUESTIONS FOR THE 7TH EDITION OF THE CENTRAL BANK EXECUTIVE TRAINEE EXAM 
QUESTION 3: Please fill in the blanks.

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:21.520
Please tell us why you seek new
employment at our firm.

00:04:21.520 --> 00:04:22.620
Yes, sir.

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:25.780
If I utilize my experience from the
Silver Socks investment division,

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:28.790
OTIS RAY

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:28.800
and take advantage of this
company's universe-wide network...

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:30.630
I have brought my plans for economic control

00:04:30.630 --> 00:04:34.300
through manipulating stock prices with
a focus on planetary takeover.

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:37.170
Looking at this as a long-term strategy to be 
carried out over the course of the next ten years...

00:04:35.240 --> 00:04:41.440
This is Mr. Ray, who has been appointed 
head of the new ventures division <i>as</i> of today.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:46.180
My name is Otis Ray.
Nice to be working with you all.

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:50.550
I'd like to start right away by having you all take a
look at this business plan I have drawn up.

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:52.810
Planetary Mine Excavation Project
in the Upsilon Star System

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:56.750
According to the report made by the
Primary Planetary Survey Commission...

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:56.060
Upsilon System

00:04:57.590 --> 00:05:01.260
To make himself accepted among
the Central Bank employees,

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:04.470
who have a very strong sense of superiority,

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:07.490
Bruce put a lot of energy into his work there.

00:05:15.340 --> 00:05:18.870
Of course he never forgot about his true purpose.

00:05:20.210 --> 00:05:21.710
GIGABANKS DESIGN SKETCH

00:05:20.550 --> 00:05:26.050
He did not forget about the ten billion space dollars
in Central Bank's vault that he was after.

00:05:26.620 --> 00:05:30.590
It really is impressive that you visited
four planets this past month

00:05:30.590 --> 00:05:32.660
and were able to bring them all into the project.

00:05:32.660 --> 00:05:34.660
Well, it's still too early to get excited.

00:05:34.660 --> 00:05:37.370
It all hinges on approval from
the investment division.

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:39.370
It'll be all right!

00:05:39.370 --> 00:05:42.630
The bank president has a lot of
faith in you after all.

00:05:43.400 --> 00:05:45.870
Alex, I want you to fly out to planet Columbus.

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:46.910
Yes, sir.

00:05:46.910 --> 00:05:48.510
Kris, you go to Teuton.

00:05:48.510 --> 00:05:49.680
Yes, sir.

00:05:49.680 --> 00:05:51.580
You're going to have your work cut out for you.

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:52.840
Yes, sir!

00:05:53.010 --> 00:05:55.450
Bruce spent a year there,

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:58.520
produced results using his own
methods and abilities,

00:05:58.520 --> 00:06:01.150
and won their confidence.

00:06:32.890 --> 00:06:34.690
Don't move.

00:06:36.760 --> 00:06:40.660
It's me! Me, Swamp!

00:06:43.830 --> 00:06:46.800
C'mon, man, don't joke around like that!

00:06:47.770 --> 00:06:50.360
Long time, no see, Swamp.

00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:54.680
Hey, have you porked out again or what?

00:06:54.680 --> 00:06:58.110
Jeez, that's a heck of a greeting after
not seeing me for so long.

00:07:00.280 --> 00:07:05.900
So then, I take it that's our mark
this time around?

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:09.960
Yep, that's it all right.

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:12.450
I'd say this is the ultimate job.

00:07:12.960 --> 00:07:15.100
It really is amazing.

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:16.890
It's amazing, but at the same time...

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:22.130
This is...

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:24.910
This is Central Bank's vault,
said to be the universe's most difficult,

00:07:24.910 --> 00:07:29.740
or even impossible, to break into, even though no
one even knows what makes it impossible!

00:07:29.980 --> 00:07:33.080
These are the blueprints for the old Gigabanks.

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:36.280
How the hell did you ever get a hold of these?!

00:07:36.720 --> 00:07:39.190
This is only the first step.

00:07:39.190 --> 00:07:43.090
See, there's this certain place where I'm now having
a certain something made using these plans.

00:07:43.590 --> 00:07:45.260
Certain something?

00:07:45.260 --> 00:07:48.390
Hey, you just look forward to seeing it, all right?

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:52.530
Your role in this has also been decided already.

00:07:52.530 --> 00:07:56.240
Whoa, now hold on! I haven't even
decided I'm doing this yet!

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:59.410
A job this big only comes once in a lifetime.

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:02.100
I don't know that I'm even ready for it.

00:08:02.940 --> 00:08:04.880
You do have a point there.

00:08:05.810 --> 00:08:08.750
I hear you, I really do.

00:08:14.460 --> 00:08:18.060
I've finished my usual rounds.

00:08:18.060 --> 00:08:20.080
All right, good work.

00:08:21.530 --> 00:08:24.520
That shows the patrol routes...

00:08:24.100 --> 00:08:26.150
Security Area Surveillance Map

00:08:24.520 --> 00:08:28.740
as well as the locations of all the surveillance
cameras along the way to Gigabanks.

00:08:30.170 --> 00:08:31.910
Perfect.

00:08:31.910 --> 00:08:33.410
You did a good job.

00:08:33.410 --> 00:08:35.170
It's no big deal.

00:08:35.380 --> 00:08:37.450
By the way, Swamp...

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:38.680
Huh?

00:08:38.680 --> 00:08:42.550
You think you could take time off
at some point next week?

00:08:42.550 --> 00:08:45.420
Sure, I guess so.

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:48.880
There's a little something I want to show you.

00:08:49.820 --> 00:08:52.390
I called Hank and Norman too.

00:08:52.390 --> 00:08:53.730
Seriously?

00:08:53.730 --> 00:08:56.400
We're finally getting to the good part.

00:08:56.400 --> 00:08:57.490
Yeah...

00:08:59.330 --> 00:09:00.870
Where's this?

00:09:00.870 --> 00:09:03.040
That's Graceland, the way it used to be.

00:09:03.040 --> 00:09:05.900
Doesn't look a thing like
the Graceland we know now.

00:09:22.360 --> 00:09:24.290
D-Boni!

00:09:26.430 --> 00:09:30.530
Let me introduce the last member
taking part in this operation.

00:09:30.530 --> 00:09:33.000
This is D-Boni.

00:09:33.070 --> 00:09:34.540
Yo!

00:09:39.810 --> 00:09:43.040
Show him the item, D-Boni.

00:10:06.630 --> 00:10:08.400
What the heck is that?

00:10:08.400 --> 00:10:13.910
It's a scale replica of Central Bank's vault,
or "Gigabanks" as it's nicknamed.

00:10:13.910 --> 00:10:15.710
That thing's a vault?

00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:17.210
Yeah...

00:10:17.210 --> 00:10:23.240
This is a 1:1000 scale model of Gigabanks that
Bruce gave me at the time as a kind of memento.

00:10:23.520 --> 00:10:27.960
Gigabanks is constructed of twelve fixed
and fifty moveable sections,

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:31.360
and the movable sections rotate
using the fixed parts as axes.

00:10:31.630 --> 00:10:33.890
The vault's distinguishing characteristic is this:

00:10:33.890 --> 00:10:37.030
any withdrawals or deposits can only be processed
through the unit's "center ball,"

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:40.700
but since the five sections that contain funds
are assembled on the vault's surface level,

00:10:40.700 --> 00:10:45.270
and then directly connected to the funds
transfer room via elevator,

00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:50.680
the operator of the vault is never able to come
into direct contact with those funds.

00:10:51.010 --> 00:10:52.580
Care for a look inside?

00:10:52.580 --> 00:10:53.840
Huh?

00:11:04.990 --> 00:11:07.030
What the hell is that?

00:11:07.030 --> 00:11:10.500
Don't ask me any questions as to why
they'd make a vault like this.

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:12.530
The thing you need to be sure to remember

00:11:12.530 --> 00:11:17.840
is that Gigabanks is reshuffled after each
authentication and also once every thirty minutes.

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:20.470
Even if you do manage to break into it,

00:11:20.470 --> 00:11:23.640
the moment you lose your bearings it's all over.

00:11:23.640 --> 00:11:27.210
It will then become a maze you'll
spend the rest of eternity in.

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:30.610
A regular Hotel California, huh?

00:11:30.990 --> 00:11:34.360
Well then, I guess I'll have me
a little look inside too.

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:36.590
Whoa, man, cut it out!

00:11:36.590 --> 00:11:38.260
I made this thing to serve as a simulation.

00:11:38.260 --> 00:11:40.820
What's the point if I don't actually use it then?

00:11:41.060 --> 00:11:45.370
Plus, it cost me at least a hundred
million space dollars to build it.

00:11:45.370 --> 00:11:48.300
A hundred million space dollars?!

00:11:48.300 --> 00:11:51.440
I guess you could say it's like the money
he put into the pot to play.

00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:54.280
You could buy a used space battleship
for that kind of money.

00:11:54.280 --> 00:11:58.150
But why did he go to the trouble of
building a copy of Gigabanks

00:11:58.150 --> 00:12:00.840
somewhere as remote as Graceland?

00:12:01.250 --> 00:12:03.750
You'd think it'd have been easier
if he had done it on a closer planet.

00:12:03.750 --> 00:12:05.020
Yeah, exactly!

00:12:05.020 --> 00:12:08.390
Then we wouldn't have had to
go through all this trouble.

00:12:09.590 --> 00:12:12.820
It's because that's the planet he met Mama on.

00:12:13.430 --> 00:12:14.630
Huh?

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:17.030
I'm sure that's why...

00:12:36.850 --> 00:12:38.550
Take a look at this.

00:12:39.050 --> 00:12:42.660
In all, there are four security measures
that stand between us and Gigabanks.

00:12:42.660 --> 00:12:45.490
First, there's the master key.

00:12:47.360 --> 00:12:49.130
Next, there's a voiceprint.

00:12:49.130 --> 00:12:52.580
The rain in Spain falls mainly on the plain.

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:53.290
SOUND SPECTROGRAM 
IComponent Feature Individual 
Processing Extraction    Matching    Identification

00:12:52.460 --> 00:12:53.330
ANALYZING

00:12:53.250 --> 00:12:54.120
MATCH

00:12:53.930 --> 00:12:55.960
Then there's a retinal scan.

00:12:55.710 --> 00:12:57.630
RETINAL AUTHENTICATION 
 Component Feature Individual 
Processing Extraction    Matching    Identification

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:57.630
ANALYZING

00:12:57.540 --> 00:12:58.420
MATCH

00:12:58.470 --> 00:13:00.340
Finally, there's a vascular scan.

00:13:00.340 --> 00:13:02.130
VASCULAR AUTHENTICATION 
Block Feature Individual 
Processing Extraction   Matching   Identification

00:13:01.260 --> 00:13:02.130
ANALYZING

00:13:02.050 --> 00:13:02.840
MATCH

00:13:04.310 --> 00:13:07.340
After that, you're as good as into Gigabanks.

00:13:07.820 --> 00:13:11.180
But the bank president's probably the only one
who can get through all that.

00:13:11.490 --> 00:13:15.290
A three-tiered biometric authentication process
is one hell of a hurdle for us to have to clear!

00:13:15.290 --> 00:13:18.660
C'mon, man, I've already thought up a plan for that.

00:13:26.300 --> 00:13:27.370
What is it?

00:13:27.370 --> 00:13:29.500
Mr. Ray is here to see you, sir.

00:13:29.500 --> 00:13:31.030
Okay, let him in.

00:13:31.610 --> 00:13:33.270
Pardon the intrusion.

00:13:34.780 --> 00:13:37.040
Hey, there, Otis!

00:13:37.040 --> 00:13:40.110
Here is the mid-term report regarding the project.

00:13:40.110 --> 00:13:41.280
Nice work.

00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:49.360
Hmm... Three out of four mines anticipate over a
two hundred percent profit increase within two years.

00:13:49.360 --> 00:13:51.160
Ah, I see, I see...

00:13:51.160 --> 00:13:53.790
Nice, very nice indeed!

00:14:29.100 --> 00:14:32.430
Hey, how's it going, D-Boni?

00:14:36.640 --> 00:14:38.700
This is a nice piece of work.

00:14:41.880 --> 00:14:44.610
I see, no good, huh?

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:47.480
Well, I'm sure you'll figure something out.

00:14:49.750 --> 00:14:52.480
Then, finally, on the evening before the heist...

00:14:52.820 --> 00:14:59.280
Synchronize your watches to 20:15 in 3... 2... 1!

00:15:00.290 --> 00:15:02.360
We'll carry things out as planned.

00:15:02.360 --> 00:15:04.420
Meet at Central Bank.

00:15:08.300 --> 00:15:09.050
MISTER

00:15:14.710 --> 00:15:16.040
Yeah?

00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:18.170
Is this Bruce?

00:15:18.980 --> 00:15:20.910
It is you, isn't it?

00:15:21.550 --> 00:15:23.140
Yeah...

00:15:23.720 --> 00:15:27.050
So why the sudden call?

00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:31.290
Tomorrow, I'm hitting Central Bank.

00:15:35.060 --> 00:15:37.460
Aren't you going to say anything?

00:15:37.460 --> 00:15:40.160
What do you want me to say?

00:15:40.500 --> 00:15:43.630
If you say you're gonna do it,
then you're gonna do it, right?

00:15:44.610 --> 00:15:46.470
That's the truth!

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:51.980
Just be sure you come home after the party.

00:15:55.450 --> 00:15:57.110
Right...

00:15:57.280 --> 00:16:00.390
Oh, hey, that reminds me,
I ran into Little Bear a while back.

00:16:00.390 --> 00:16:02.920
You mean that guy's still alive?!

00:16:02.920 --> 00:16:05.480
Yup, and he hasn't changed a bit.

00:16:13.370 --> 00:16:14.330
Action!

00:16:14.570 --> 00:16:15.040
Good morning.

00:16:15.040 --> 00:16:15.970
Good morning.
Good morning.

00:16:15.970 --> 00:16:16.440
Good morning.

00:16:16.440 --> 00:16:18.640
Ordinarily, the five vault rooms,

00:16:18.640 --> 00:16:21.080
which is to say all of the money in Gigabanks,

00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:23.310
do not all come together on the uppermost level.

00:16:23.310 --> 00:16:25.210
There is, however, one exception.

00:16:25.210 --> 00:16:26.980
Good morning, Mr. Ray!

00:16:26.980 --> 00:16:30.510
In the case of a large earthquake,
fire or other unforeseen event,

00:16:27.250 --> 00:16:28.750
MAGNITUDE 7.9

00:16:30.350 --> 00:16:32.320
Disaster Response 
Emergency Program 

00:16:30.590 --> 00:16:33.190
an emergency program is automatically initiated

00:16:33.190 --> 00:16:35.690
and all of the funds are assembled
on the surface level of the vault,

00:16:35.690 --> 00:16:38.560
so that they can be carried off to a safe location.

00:16:39.460 --> 00:16:41.050
Good morning.

00:16:46.070 --> 00:16:49.470
Hey, good morning, Otis!

00:16:52.040 --> 00:16:53.610
Hey, it's me.

00:16:53.610 --> 00:16:56.080
Don't let anyone in here for the next hour.

00:16:56.080 --> 00:16:58.070
No phone calls either.

00:16:58.850 --> 00:17:00.440
Understood, sir.

00:17:02.480 --> 00:17:04.220
It's the bank president.

00:17:04.220 --> 00:17:06.990
Well, no need to report if it's the president.

00:17:06.990 --> 00:17:09.080
Yeah, I guess you're right.

00:17:27.910 --> 00:17:30.680
The rain in Spain falls mainly on the plain.

00:17:28.150 --> 00:17:30.820
SOUND SPECTROGRAM 
Component Feature Individual 
Processing Extraction   Matching   Identification

00:17:29.940 --> 00:17:30.820
ANALYZING

00:17:30.730 --> 00:17:31.650
MATCH

00:17:40.660 --> 00:17:42.580
RETINAL AUTHENTICATION 
 Component Feature Individual 
Processing Extraction    Matching    Identification

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:42.580
ANALYZING

00:17:42.500 --> 00:17:43.200
MATCH

00:17:50.400 --> 00:17:53.400
Huh? The president's gone all the way
to the last checkpoint.

00:17:53.400 --> 00:17:56.340
I'm telling you there's no need to report it!

00:18:06.510 --> 00:18:08.070
Ah, it's back on.

00:18:08.220 --> 00:18:10.180
The president's not there.

00:18:10.180 --> 00:18:12.390
He probably went into the center ball.

00:18:12.390 --> 00:18:15.250
That's the only place where there are
no surveillance cameras.

00:18:52.630 --> 00:18:54.060
Wild!

00:18:54.060 --> 00:18:56.530
So that is the center of Gigabanks?

00:18:56.530 --> 00:18:57.600
That's right.

00:18:57.600 --> 00:19:01.430
There's only one person in the world
who's seen it from that angle.

00:19:33.270 --> 00:19:34.370
Bingo!

00:19:34.370 --> 00:19:36.000
What happened?!

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:39.210
It looks like there's been an explosion in Gigabanks!

00:19:39.210 --> 00:19:40.470
What?!

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:42.490
Disaster Response 
Emergency Program

00:19:40.530 --> 00:19:42.490
INITIATED

00:19:46.080 --> 00:19:49.170
You're excused! Both of you get down there too!

00:19:49.380 --> 00:19:50.650
Yessir!

00:19:50.650 --> 00:19:52.790
In the event of a first-degree disaster,

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:55.660
Gigabanks automatically initiates a program
to release all of its money

00:19:55.660 --> 00:19:59.150
by shuffling all sections containing
funds to the top level.

00:20:29.190 --> 00:20:30.660
Thank you for coming!

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:32.930
We've come here to recover the funds

00:20:32.930 --> 00:20:35.400
in accordance with what's outlined
in the disaster response manual.

00:20:43.240 --> 00:20:44.730
This way!

00:20:56.720 --> 00:20:59.150
All right then, it's safely in our custody.

00:20:59.150 --> 00:21:01.050
Ah... Right!

00:21:11.630 --> 00:21:13.360
Huh?

00:21:13.430 --> 00:21:15.170
What's he...

00:21:15.170 --> 00:21:17.760
Is this... No, it couldn't be!

00:21:19.410 --> 00:21:21.580
Mr. Ray?

00:21:21.580 --> 00:21:22.540
Huh?!

00:21:27.710 --> 00:21:30.120
Mr. Ray!

00:21:30.250 --> 00:21:31.340
No way...

00:21:34.920 --> 00:21:37.920
That rocks! That totally rocks!

00:21:37.920 --> 00:21:40.090
It's too much. That's friggin' hilarious!

00:21:40.090 --> 00:21:42.220
That guy's unreal!
It's too much. That's friggin' hilarious!

00:21:46.130 --> 00:21:51.200
Well, there's your complete record
of the Central Bank heist.

00:22:01.110 --> 00:22:04.720
So how about it? It's going to be one hell of a job.

00:22:04.720 --> 00:22:07.190
You still wanna go?

00:22:07.190 --> 00:22:09.790
How can you even ask that now?

00:22:09.790 --> 00:22:11.550
The answer's obvious.

00:22:17.350 --> 00:22:21.500
<i>Where are these waterdrops</i>

00:22:21.500 --> 00:22:31.810
<i>that travel along my cheek coming from?</i>

00:22:32.080 --> 00:22:35.940
<i>Tell me...</i>

00:22:38.540 --> 00:22:49.630
<i>I grabbed the rule that says we can't tum back time</i>

00:22:49.630 --> 00:22:56.310
<i>by the collar</i>

00:22:57.140 --> 00:23:00.770
<i>I resist the fading memories</i>

00:23:00.770 --> 00:23:11.420
<i>even with the feelings here</i>

00:23:11.420 --> 00:23:14.920
<i>But I'm sure they'll come to kill me</i>

00:23:15.290 --> 00:23:21.530
<i>From out of all the days that have gone by</i>

00:23:21.530 --> 00:23:30.000
<i>there's only one thing I can believe in</i>

00:23:30.130 --> 00:23:36.340
<i>I cried until my voice was hoarse</i>

00:23:36.340 --> 00:23:39.680
<i>Come to me</i>

00:23:39.680 --> 00:23:43.350
<i>Be by my side</i>

00:23:43.350 --> 00:23:46.980
<i>O Kay?</i>

00:23:50.590 --> 00:23:54.960
After that, Bruce gave each of us
the cut we had agreed on.

00:23:54.960 --> 00:23:59.990
He put the rest in a vault on Graceland
and sealed it away.

00:24:01.870 --> 00:24:04.530
So how did this latest job go?

00:24:05.970 --> 00:24:08.240
It was a blast.
